<title>INDIA: YIELD ON INDIA 91-DAY T-BILL EASES TO 6.65 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>YIELD ON INDIA 91-DAY T-BILL EASES TO 6.65 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off rate of 98.37 rupees at an auction of 91-day treasury bills on Friday.</p>
<p>This is a shade higher than the 98.36 rupee cut-off rate set at the last auction.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield worked out to 6.65 percent, down from 6.69 percent at the last auction. </p>
